    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2016-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The total of the four cousin ages is \\(4\\cdot8=32\\). Since the median is \\(5\\), the two middle ages have average \\(5\\), so their sum is \\(10\\).\n\nTherefore the youngest and oldest ages sum to \\(32-10=22\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
